# Cline Rules: NSdocs Document Consumption Module

## Implementation Patterns

### Code Organization
1. **Solution Structure**
   - Clean separation of projects
   - Feature-based organization in each layer
   - Consistent naming conventions
   - Clear dependency flow

2. **Domain Model Standards**
   - Strong typing with enums for known values
   - 44-character access key validation
   - Proper entity relationships
   - Value objects when appropriate

3. **CQRS Implementation**
   - Commands for mutations
   - Queries for reads
   - MediatR pipeline behaviors
   - Validation before handling
   - Boolean return for update/delete operations

4. **Event Design**
   - Base event class with common properties
   - Specific event classes for each operation
   - Previous values in update events
   - Event publishing after successful operations

5. **Event-Driven Architecture**
   - Publish events for document changes
   - Process events asynchronously
   - Update consumption in worker service
   - Decouple document and consumption operations

### Development Guidelines
1. **Documentation Priority**
   - Update memory bank before code
   - Document technical decisions
   - Track progress per checkpoint
   - Clear success criteria

2. **Testing Approach**
   - Test-driven development
   - Integration tests for events
   - Performance benchmarks
   - Checkpoint validation

## Critical Paths

### API Operations
1. **Document Management**
   ```
   # Create Document
   POST /api/documents
   {
     "accessKey": "44-digit-key",
     "companyId": 123,
     "origin": "file|email|ws",
     "documentType": "nfe|cte|etc",
     "status": "ok|pending|error|non-existing"
   }
   
   # Update Document
   PUT /api/documents/{id}
   {
     "id": 1,
     "accessKey": "44-digit-key",
     "companyId": 123,
     "origin": "file|email|ws",
     "documentType": "nfe|cte|etc",
     "status": "ok|pending|error|non-existing"
   }
   
   # Delete Document
   DELETE /api/documents/{id}
   ```

2. **Event Publishing**
   ```csharp
   // Base event class
   public abstract class DocumentEventBase
   {
       public long DocumentId { get; set; }
       public int CompanyId { get; set; }
       public string AccessKey { get; set; } = string.Empty;
       public DateTime RequestDate { get; set; }
       public DocumentOrigin Origin { get; set; }
       public DocumentType DocumentType { get; set; }
       public DocumentStatus Status { get; set; }
   }

   // Specific events
   public class DocumentCreatedEvent : DocumentEventBase { }
   
   public class DocumentUpdatedEvent : DocumentEventBase 
   {
       public DocumentOrigin PreviousOrigin { get; set; }
       public DocumentStatus PreviousStatus { get; set; }
       public int PreviousCompanyId { get; set; }
   }
   
   public class DocumentDeletedEvent : DocumentEventBase { }
   ```

3. **Worker Processing with MassTransit**
   ```csharp
   // MassTransit Consumer pattern
   public class DocumentCreatedConsumer : IConsumer<DocumentCreatedEvent>
   {
       private readonly ILogger<DocumentCreatedConsumer> _logger;
       private readonly IApplicationDbContext _context;

       public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<DocumentCreatedEvent> context)
       {
           var @event = context.Message;
           
           // Get or create consumption record for the month
           var consumptionDate = new DateTime(@event.RequestDate.Year, @event.RequestDate.Month, 1);
           
           var consumption = await _context.Consumptions
               .FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => 
                   c.CompanyId == @event.CompanyId &&
                   c.ConsumptionDate == consumptionDate &&
                   c.Origin == @event.Origin &&
                   c.DocumentType == @event.DocumentType &&
                   c.Status == @event.Status);
           
           // Update consumption logic
           // ...
           
           await _context.SaveChangesAsync(context.CancellationToken);
       }
   }
   
   // Similar consumers for DocumentUpdatedEvent and DocumentDeletedEvent
   ```

## Implementation Guidelines

### Command Handling with Event Publishing
```csharp
// Create Command Handler
public class CreateDocumentCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<CreateDocumentCommand, long>
{
    private readonly IApplicationDbContext _context;
    private readonly IEventPublisher _eventPublisher;

    public async Task<long> Handle(CreateDocumentCommand request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // Create document
        var document = new Document { ... };
        _context.Documents.Add(document);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);

        // Publish event
        await _eventPublisher.PublishAsync(new DocumentCreatedEvent
        {
            DocumentId = document.Id,
            CompanyId = document.CompanyId,
            // Other properties...
        }, cancellationToken);

        return document.Id;
    }
}

// Update Command Handler
public class UpdateDocumentCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<UpdateDocumentCommand, bool>
{
    private readonly IApplicationDbContext _context;
    private readonly IEventPublisher _eventPublisher;

    public async Task<bool> Handle(UpdateDocumentCommand request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var document = await _context.Documents
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(d => d.Id == request.Id, cancellationToken);

        if (document == null)
        {
            return false;
        }

        // Store previous values
        var previousCompanyId = document.CompanyId;
        var previousOrigin = document.Origin;
        var previousStatus = document.Status;

        // Update document
        document.CompanyId = request.CompanyId;
        // Other properties...
        
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);

        // Publish event if relevant fields changed
        if (previousCompanyId != document.CompanyId || 
            previousOrigin != document.Origin || 
            previousStatus != document.Status)
        {
            await _eventPublisher.PublishAsync(new DocumentUpdatedEvent
            {
                DocumentId = document.Id,
                // Other properties...
                PreviousCompanyId = previousCompanyId,
                PreviousOrigin = previousOrigin,
                PreviousStatus = previousStatus
            }, cancellationToken);
        }

        return true;
    }
}

// Delete Command Handler
public class DeleteDocumentCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<DeleteDocumentCommand, bool>
{
    private readonly IApplicationDbContext _context;
    private readonly IEventPublisher _eventPublisher;

    public async Task<bool> Handle(DeleteDocumentCommand request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var document = await _context.Documents
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(d => d.Id == request.Id, cancellationToken);

        if (document == null)
        {
            return false;
        }

        // Store document data for the event
        var documentEvent = new DocumentDeletedEvent
        {
            DocumentId = document.Id,
            // Other properties...
        };

        // Delete document
        _context.Documents.Remove(document);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);

        // Publish event
        await _eventPublisher.PublishAsync(documentEvent, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

### Event Publishing
```csharp
// Event Publisher Interface
public interface IEventPublisher
{
    Task PublishAsync<TEvent>(TEvent @event, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) where TEvent : class;
}

// In-Memory Implementation
public class InMemoryEventPublisher : IEventPublisher
{
    private readonly ILogger<InMemoryEventPublisher> _logger;

    public Task PublishAsync<TEvent>(TEvent @event, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) where TEvent : class
    {
        _logger.LogInformation("Event published: {EventType} - {EventData}", typeof(TEvent).Name, @event);
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}

// RabbitMQ Implementation with MassTransit
public class RabbitMQEventPublisher : IEventPublisher
{
    private readonly ILogger<RabbitMQEventPublisher> _logger;
    private readonly IBus _bus;
    private readonly RabbitMQOptions _options;

    public RabbitMQEventPublisher(
        ILogger<RabbitMQEventPublisher> logger,
        IBus bus,
        IOptions<RabbitMQOptions> options)
    {
        _logger = logger;
        _bus = bus;
        _options = options.Value;
    }

    public async Task PublishAsync<TEvent>(TEvent @event, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) where TEvent : class
    {
        try
        {
            // Publish message using MassTransit
            await _bus.Publish(@event, cancellationToken);
            
            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Event published to RabbitMQ using MassTransit: {EventType}", 
                typeof(TEvent).Name);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to publish event to RabbitMQ");
            throw;
        }
    }
}
```

## Project Evolution

### Phase Guidelines
1. **API Setup**
   - Focus on core domain models
   - Basic CRUD operations
   - Entity configurations
   - Repository pattern

2. **CQRS Integration**
   - Command/Query separation
